{"title":"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">2025 AMC 10B #23</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2025 AMC 12B #19</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_23\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 23</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Easier_way_to_count)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Easier way to count)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(0-indexing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (0-indexing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(faster_ending)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (faster ending)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:55)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:55)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_StressedPineapple\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by StressedPineapple</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_OmegaLearn.org\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by OmegaLearn.org</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_5_by_MadMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 5 by MadMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_23\">Problem 23</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 23\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangular grid of squares has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/80401851927344d980a3cea9388530b9a9f1b065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$141$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> rows and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd34ff50f8bba26a08bc96a69e921daa60f5f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> columns. Each square has room for two numbers. Horace and Vera each fill in the grid by putting the numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/d/fbdfc9603c9563aff0babdf16e87e5e41c273cbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$141 \\times 91 = 12{,}831$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"17\" /> into the squares. Horace fills the grid horizontally: he puts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd34ff50f8bba26a08bc96a69e921daa60f5f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> in order from left to right into row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, puts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/403d424cf0f48517174037a871a71d9c35f1796e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$92$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea9119513dcfff6adda7e89a8f0aa460eaed0305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$182$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> into row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in order from left to right, and continues similarly through row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/80401851927344d980a3cea9388530b9a9f1b065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$141$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Vera fills the grid vertically: she puts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/80401851927344d980a3cea9388530b9a9f1b065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$141$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> in order from top to bottom into column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce8614c1b3993e78519131182767d0a43ea0714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/ead8ea40efad9858229067e6824c5cb06c5afc6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$282$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> into column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in order from top to bottom, and continues similarly through column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd34ff50f8bba26a08bc96a69e921daa60f5f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. How many squares get two copies of the same number?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa9fc192286ac9eb354b11b8b05ca70225eeb9a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~7 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}~10 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}~11 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}~12 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}~19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This problem is similar to problem 16 on the 2000 AMC 12. The other problem asks for the sum of the duplicates, not the number of them.\n~mathwizard123123\n</p><p>Yes, and it feels like this 2025 problem is a bit easier.\n~heliostan\n</p><p>Yes, I agree. \n~Cheerfulfrog\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is one of the numbers that got written twice in the same box. Suppose it is at column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. We will write an expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in two ways: from Horace's perspective and Vera's perspective.\n</p><p>From Horace's perspective, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/8418986621fc247b9897482f3f18d34d0bfe06bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = (y-1)(141) + x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" />. This is because there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851018537a4268dffd3e893158af5b7d9f3aeb0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> full rows before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and we then need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> more numbers to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Similarly, Vera will say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffa870a9481648e30d9c74fa59021c06df90fd05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = (x-1)(91) + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We now have the Diophantine equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89030cd8a525733be097c9f998caa53da3e719d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(y-1)(141) + x = (x-1)(91)+y\\]\" width=\"271\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ef8c39a1bd1866e01e37009af043380f6e02ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[141y-141+x = 91x-91+y\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd1beecb84695828f8334ec4f45f7a39740b883c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[140y=90x+50\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa513a72741fcd6a5f3e6fe3b502555a50c8c23.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[14y = 9x + 5\\]\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" />\nOne such solution is, of course, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/915f1781caa8b3e0eddafe7a445019f06178da22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. We find further solutions by adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. For example, the second solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/b/81b5db985e72547066f8eb28f1c86c4c6a584b5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(15,10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />. This continues until <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/001fc053497b486e9e59b37a8135fb320496bc03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(141,91)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" /> is reached. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd34aa5e4f49c065b66db919bf81d6d611bc2bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> ordered pairs in this list.\n</p><p>~lprado\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Easier_way_to_count.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Easier_way_to_count)\">Solution 1 (Easier way to count)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Easier way to count)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The Diophantine equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fef0c5785c14fd80ba7d9e657cd186c6a4b617a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14y-9x=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" /> is in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32d7893d1d274dbffd64b00d9735437786f01269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax+by = c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /> has primary solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb4df56d4212732f01473f613ea91f2c35eb6ec7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_0, y_0) = (1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45e6e6012e30e31ea0e5667e4052ad8cc5cecc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = \\gcd(a,b) =\\gcd(14, -5) = \\gcd(14,5) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"353\" height=\"20\" />, and thus the solutions are of the form\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/20188485825f62dbe9af5c064a6ec69faeea0533.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = 1 + 9k\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fef47f1b3388ef10499a74d2cb8859a4bccf7f17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 1 + 14k\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Then, notice that because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb745f62ddf5625f47a60b8976c60faebcf74f43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b644759f8e151a9a9bc223018df09364d63cef07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le x \\le 141$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/c/d3c432e76846ffab010c50f773f1bfcb67295205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le y \\le 91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />, the largest value possible is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b98641f534d2ff6d18ec65d976bfacb8e3ba4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y) = (141, 91)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />, and thus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/134b2c18db419d55a41cfe655736782f3b538dc7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[14k \\le 140\\]\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f0843131e820153a9f5a1224e31ba520fd200b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9k \\le 90\\]\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>In which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/b/66b31c6ce30e39285cb2adaeda39b27d38c66d29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\le 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> in both cases. Thus there are 10 positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfy the following. Including 0, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/484c0121fcca1c41a99fdc3f5d0d18b8d8e658cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 + 1 = \\boxed{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.280-indexing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(0-indexing)\">Solution 2 (0-indexing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (0-indexing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For these types of problems, we essentially analyze residues, so it is more convenient to work with 0-indexing: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13cac8a5cd36330543c671ee30f2f1a1b6091337.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=0,1,2,\\dots,90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/986b87b545bdbdc75aa70d7cc6af95d4dc9ad9cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=0,1,2,\\dots,140$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9adbd35665009b1024e8457f086bdca263ebb2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=91r+c+1=141c+r+1\\iff 9r=14c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"369\" height=\"15\" />. We must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f72f3e861bb68b316c75304b890caefa452dfae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,c)=(0,0),(14,9),(28,18),\\dots,(140,90)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"337\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb53f7351e597b13dbe72bc1552d37522c2f827.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{ \\textbf{(C)}~11 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~imosilver\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28faster_ending.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(faster_ending)\">Solution 2 (faster ending)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (faster ending)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After indexing to 0, we imagine a line that passes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/4/5f4d6b5a651a465c43ca270543b92bf5dcf760da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(140,90)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />. We know we are looking for all lattice points that lie on this line (this intuitively makes sense, because any points above the line would have column numbers far ahead of the rows, and vice versa). \n</p><p>Therefore, we know that the number of points must divide both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b51850ccd3440214d4ccfbc14d29b2a31bfda55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$140$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The GCD of the two is 10. We also account for point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, and get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f67e3f74eac5086e1bcf1538d61e947fe38f62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+1=\\boxed{ \\textbf{(C)}~11 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"139\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that Horaces number can be expressed as the remainder of the row number plus the column number so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />(Horaces Number)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d66f72b609fbd6d52ed4d8a52b2e249bd174631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=91(c-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />(column addition)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e127fd5d84195d158cd346577b9a505e2d514864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />(remainder of division) and do the same for Vera <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4d8fb1d7ccb234ec23f3d888cfb91480883d7c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V=141(r-1)+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" />.The condition is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3de140a88e8da67d4cb315da12d17068277faf6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H=V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> so set the equations equal to each other. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/d/0ad0b8ecbc7279a7f1172975c18170a943db3f5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91(c-1)+r=141(r-1)+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"240\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2fda19d4b2ff56186bf437d9bcbd8d28a86c879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91c-91+r=141r-141+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"239\" height=\"15\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56f5e7ff4df4b2fe4ff251ce5a08712a6657ac7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$140r=90c+50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"129\" height=\"15\" />.This a linear Diophantine equation and the 1st solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7a465ffe5255961382f5777569608be052b783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> where the solution repeats every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a914330e143d92ae560262277c3329beb6395693.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$lcm(90,140)=1260$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" /> there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> solutions so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e19053839f0c911efef1a33882b28a50647a0bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"60\" height=\"30\" /> is correct.\n</p><p>~~TFEA\n</p><p>~<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/latex.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\LaTeX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> by OlympiadMaster\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E0:55.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:55)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:55)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:55)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/X5nwdzpKb98\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/X5nwdzpKb98</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gsjsWaDAFnY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gsjsWaDAFnY</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dy7D9Ma3_XY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dy7D9Ma3_XY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_StressedPineapple\">Video Solution 2 by StressedPineapple</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by StressedPineapple\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=xCG1ftJq5x0\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=xCG1ftJq5x0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_OmegaLearn.org\">Video Solution 3 by OmegaLearn.org</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by OmegaLearn.org\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/MpOLJM1GjYQ\">https://youtu.be/MpOLJM1GjYQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_4_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution 4 (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4 (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SDa6Zg-yahA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SDa6Zg-yahA</a>\n~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_5_by_MadMath\">Video Solution 5 by MadMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 5 by MadMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/B3mLbHraweQ\">https://youtu.be/B3mLbHraweQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B\" title